feat(recall): rewrite a missed question in the model's own words (4.5.0)

The lexical slice misses about 40% of reworded questions at 600 entries and no admission threshold
fixes it - "atlas 要发新版本" and "atlas 服务上线先走灰度" share exactly one token. A tokenizer cannot
bridge that; a model can.

Measured with an oracle rather than a fixture, because a fixture would measure the fixture: of the
questions the slice missed, 100% would be recovered by a correct rewrite - 76 of 76 at 200 entries,
115 of 115 at 600. That settles the design question (rewriting is sufficient in principle) and
leaves only how close a real model gets.

The ordering in the Host is what makes this possible: systemPrompt.assemble runs before the
agent/pre-step waterfall. A section's text is synchronous with no session, so it cannot ask a model -
but it can leave a note, and the waterfall, which can await, acts on it in time for the same turn.

Guards matter more than the feature: only on a genuine miss, once per turn, and the rescue is added
rather than substituted for what the section already said. recallRewrite defaults to on-miss, costing
one model call per missed turn and nothing on a hit.

Rejected: paragraph-long "queries" (a paragraph means the model did something else), a single line of
prose (it means the model declined), and rewriting on every turn (cost, and the risk of replacing a
right answer).

287 tests, coverage lines 89.1 / branches 70.1 / functions 83.0.
